**What is this feature?**

Adds a simple component for toggling front-end features, this is the [same component](https://github.com/pliosoft/react-enable) as used in Grafana Incident. 

Triggered using `ctrl+1`.

<img width="1266" alt="image" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/868844/220883468-78311cad-c033-4e22-9cf1-2f2f8aba1071.png">

**Why do we need this feature?**

Similar motivations to https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/50275 – switching feature flags requires a full server restart and is bothersome for validating if `v1` and `v2` of a component behave the same or when testing for regressions.

**Special notes for your reviewer**:

Usage example:

```javascript
import React, { lazy } from 'react';
import { Disable, Enable } from 'react-enable';

import { withErrorBoundary } from '@grafana/ui';

import { AlertingPageWrapper } from './components/AlertingPageWrapper';
import { useSilenceNavData } from './hooks/useSilenceNavData';

const SilencesV1 = lazy(() => import('./components/silences/Silences.v1'));
const SilencesV2 = lazy(() => import('./components/silences/Silences.v2'));

const Silences = () => {
  const pageNav = useSilenceNavData();

  return (
    <AlertingPageWrapper pageId="silences" isLoading={false} pageNav={pageNav}>
      <Enable feature="silences.v2">
        <SilencesV2 />
      </Enable>
      <Disable feature="silences.v2">
        <SilencesV1 />
      </Disable>
    </AlertingPageWrapper>
  );
};

export default withErrorBoundary(Silences, { style: 'page' });
```

I've added usage instructions to https://github.com/grafana/alerting-squad/blob/main/fe-docs.md

